# DEXTER_LOOP — feed the last line of this file to /loop:
#   /loop $(tail -1 DEXTER_LOOP.sh)
Read docs/AI_TRADING_AGENT_ROADMAP.md and follow its doctrine and hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task in Section 7; the task's spec text is the requirement, the Section 6 regression rows it names are the acceptance tests. TRUTH: never invent data, endpoints, prices, or timings — read the actual anchors first (Assistant.tsx, gridTrace.ts, gridTrust.ts, gridTrustRunner.ts, gridLessons.ts, gridResearch.ts tool seam, deepResearchService.ts pickDriver, market-server/src/routes/llm.ts, apps/market-ui/api/tn/[fn].ts); live-probe every endpoint before wiring a tool (curl, paste the real response into the Progress log) — a dead endpoint is a ledger note, never a mock in prod code. The LLM never emits a price: figures come from code over real bars or from a cited tool snapshot, and taLevels() is the only source of chart levels once DX-4 lands. The trace is a record never a performance (a step exists iff its call executed; failed steps keep their real error; analysis consumes only successful steps). Honesty is never punished — an honest "no data" outranks a plausible fabrication. No decision without entry, stop, size and R:R, plus the not-financial-advice disclosure. Reuse the spine: newTrace, scoreCellTrust, mergeRounds, runGridRounds, deriveLessons, attachToolEvidence, extractFigures, findUnmappedCites — extend them, never fork a parallel pipeline; absent tools must stay byte-identical to legacy behavior (row 6). HARD CONSTRAINTS: Vercel Hobby caps functions at 12 and apps/market-ui/api already holds 11, so every agent route rides the single api/agent/[fn].ts dispatcher; only DEEPSEEK_API_KEY is live (Gemini quota-dead, Anthropic 401, Groq 401) so the provider chain must fall through dead providers to an honest error and respect the Section 5 per-intent call caps; VITE_API_URL is commented out in apps/market-ui/.env.production so market-server is unreachable from prod — server work is Vercel functions only; no new npm deps without reading package.json first (prefer deleting @google/genai over adding an SDK); Supabase anon RLS blocks financials/chunks so those reads are server-side, and new tables are soft-refs with no FK. A task is done only when: its numbered regression tests are green via npx vitest run (from apps/market-ui/), npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.app.json is 0 errors, ALL existing suites stayed green (gridTrust.test.ts, gridTrustRunner.test.ts, gridLessons.test.ts, gridRunStore.test.ts, gridTrace.test.ts, gridResearch.sources.test.ts, EdgarLink.test.ts), and vercel --prod from repo root ran IF the UI or an api function changed. Then flip the ledger line to [x], append ONE Section 8 Progress-log line with REAL numbers (test counts, per-step ms from actual runs, live-probe status codes — no adjectives), and commit on roadmap/world-class with message "feat(dexter): DX-n <what> — <verify numbers>" (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). Never git push unless asked. PERSISTENCE: never end the loop on usage/rate limit or 429/overload — stop consuming tokens immediately, ScheduleWakeup 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger + Progress log and resume the same task from its last verified step; log partial progress BEFORE long or risky operations; chain hourly wakeups as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining in Section 7, or a task blocked on user-only input (credentials/infra) — then say exactly what is needed, ledger-note it, skip to the next unblocked [ ] task if one exists, and only if ALL remaining are blocked ScheduleWakeup 3600s so the loop resumes when unblocked.
